\ Build-only regression test: --emit-runtime-image successfully encodes
\ descriptors for transitively imported lib/process.1z and
\ lib/scanner.1z. The descriptor encoder previously skipped descriptor
\ entries (`inner-type`, `variants`, `field-types`, `fields`, `define`)
\ on these libraries' types (signal, stdio-mode, process, shell-safe,
\ scanner, etc.), printing `runtime-image-load-note` chains at startup.
\ The current static-C-data descriptor encoding has no skip surface;
\ this fixture asserts that the build succeeds with none of the prior
\ diagnostic notes by pinning an empty stderr in the build golden.
\
\ This fixture is build-only because executing the rehydrated lib
\ TypeValues currently trips a separate runtime SIGSEGV. The companion
\ runtime_image_lib_descriptors.1z fixture exercises the smaller
\ "import-only, run to completion" axis that the SIGSEGV does not block.
use "process" ;
use "scanner" ;
